StudyAlign — Licensing
======================

StudyAlign is a monorepo whose components are released under different
licenses. The license that applies to a file is the license of the component
directory that contains it. Each component also ships the full text of its
license in a LICENSE file inside its own directory.

Copyright (c) 2021-2026 Florian Lehmann

Per-directory split
-------------------

  libs/study-align-lib     MIT License
                           -> libs/study-align-lib/LICENSE

  apps/backend             GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (AGPL-3.0-only)
                           -> apps/backend/LICENSE

  apps/admin-frontend      GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (AGPL-3.0-only)
                           -> apps/admin-frontend/LICENSE

  apps/study-frontend      GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (AGPL-3.0-only)
                           -> apps/study-frontend/LICENSE

Default for everything else
---------------------------

The StudyAlign platform as a whole is licensed under the GNU Affero General
Public License, version 3.0 (AGPL-3.0-only). Everything in this repository that
is not inside one of the component directories listed above — top-level tooling,
deployment configuration, and documentation — is therefore covered by the
AGPL-3.0-only, with the single exception of `libs/study-align-lib`, which is the
client library and is released under the permissive MIT License so it can be
embedded freely in instrumented products and prototypes.

The full text of the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 is in each AGPL
component's LICENSE file and at https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.txt .
The MIT License text is in libs/study-align-lib/LICENSE .
